\b\fs30 Abstract\b0\fs24\par
The API-Based RAG Knowledge Chatbot is a full-stack artificial intelligence project that converts external data sources into a conversational knowledge system. The system allows authenticated users to upload PDF documents or connect REST API endpoints, process the source data, generate semantic embeddings using Gemini embedding models, store vectors in Qdrant, and ask questions through source-specific chat sessions. The generated responses are grounded in retrieved context rather than unsupported general knowledge.\par
The backend is implemented with Django and Django REST Framework. It handles authentication, source management, ingestion, PDF parsing, API fetching, embedding generation, vector indexing, retrieval, and LLM orchestration. The frontend is built using Next.js, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS, giving users an interactive dashboard for adding sources and chatting with them. The application uses PostgreSQL for relational application data in production and Qdrant as a dedicated vector database. Gemini Embeddings provide the semantic representation layer, while a Groq-hosted OpenAI-compatible chat model generates final answers from retrieved evidence.\par
This report presents the motivation, objectives, literature background, system design, implementation details, methodology, testing approach, limitations, future scope, and conclusion of the project. The future scope includes controlled website ingestion, YouTube video transcript ingestion, audio and image-based document support, hybrid search, analytics, background workers, and enterprise-level deployment features.\par
