\b\fs26 Appendix C: Sample Project Viva Questions\b0\fs24\par
Q: What is retrieval-augmented generation?\par
A: It is a method where relevant external context is retrieved first and then passed to a language model for grounded answer generation.\par
Q: Why is Qdrant used?\par
A: Qdrant is used because semantic search requires efficient vector storage and similarity search.\par
Q: Why are Gemini Embeddings used?\par
A: They convert source text and questions into semantic vectors so the system can search by meaning.\par
Q: Why use PostgreSQL and Qdrant separately?\par
A: PostgreSQL stores relational application records, while Qdrant stores vectors and performs similarity search.\par
Q: How does the system avoid unsupported answers?\par
A: The prompt instructs the model to answer only from retrieved context and to say when information is missing.\par
Q: What future input types can be added?\par
A: Website pages, YouTube transcripts, audio files, scanned documents, images, spreadsheets, and other structured data sources can be added.\par
Layer | Technology | Role in Project\par
Frontend | Next.js, React, TypeScript | Builds dashboard, login, source management, and chat screens.\par
Styling | Tailwind CSS | Provides responsive and consistent user interface styling.\par
Backend | Django, Django REST Framework | Exposes authentication, source, ingestion, and chat APIs.\par
Relational Data | PostgreSQL | Stores users, source metadata, chat sessions, and messages in production.\par
Vector Data | Qdrant | Stores embeddings and performs semantic nearest-neighbor retrieval.\par
Embeddings | Gemini Embeddings | Converts source chunks and questions into semantic vectors.\par
LLM | Groq OpenAI-compatible chat model | Generates grounded answers from retrieved context.\par
PDF Processing | pypdf | Extracts text from uploaded PDF files.\par
Deployment Support | Gunicorn, WhiteNoise, environment variables | Supports cloud deployment and production configuration.\par
